    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-133968",
      "knowledge_point_id": "79f1049a-8af9-50ee-9dac-9dbd9c19bdc6",
      "knowledge_point": "Correctly Identifying a Scatter Plot",
      "problem": "A teacher wants to determine whether a student's performance in mathematics influences their performance in physics. The following table shows the grades of $5$ students in a mathematics and physics class. \n\n| **Math Grade** | **$8$** | **$6$** | **$8$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Physics Grade** | $9$ | $5$ | $8$ | $4$ | $3$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?",
      "worked_solution": "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (math grade) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (physics grade) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/5bdbaadf2d3ea794c145365f5ee61ee4c1551dc72b62c8a681933b9aac74d214.png)",
