      "problem": "Lucy, who plays basketball, notices that the number of points she scores in a game increases as a function of the number of hours she practices her jump shot each week. She records the following data.\n\n| **Number of Hours Training** | **$4$** | **$6$** | **$7$** | **$8$** | **$10$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Points Scored per Game** | $8$ | $12$ | $16$ | $20$ | $28$ |\n\nWhich of the following scatter plots represents this data?",
      "worked_solution": "We create a scatter diagram in the coordinate plane as follows:\n\n- First, we draw the independent variable (number of hours training) along the horizontal axis.\n\n- Then, we draw the dependent variable (points scored per game) along the vertical axis.\n\n- Finally, we plot the points that correspond to the pairs from the data.\n\nThis gives us the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934290/assets/b741264e080009d9e634e7ffce5e9041b6cd65b34e4d840700397a7378255ea8.png)",
